[[2047,31,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The Air Bag system control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receives a supply\ncontrolled by the ignition (15/54) at pin 15 from the line protected\nby shunt fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 3/98 or \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B32</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 3/98.</p><p>up to 2/99 or from fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from supplementary fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98A</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>Pin 14 is connected to the specific earth \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C50</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ,\nlike pin 30, on &quot;complete&quot; versions, i.e. with a passenger\nAir Bag. (on versions with a driver&#x27;s Air Bag only, pin 30 is not\nconnected).</p><p>When an impact of a set severity (determined by the control software) is detected, the control unit sends control signals to set off the modules:</p><ul><li>to driver&#x27;s Air Bag <strong>Q9</strong> , via the steering wheel\nclockspring <strong>Q10</strong> (from pins 1 and 2):</li><li>to passenger airbag <strong>Q11</strong> (from pins 3 and 4);</li><li>to driver&#x27;s side pretensioner <strong>Q20</strong> (from pins 10\nand 11) and passenger side pretensioner <strong>Q21</strong> (from pins 6\nand 7).</li></ul>"],[2047,31,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>Pins 23 and 27 are connected to the sensor\nin the seat for disabling the passenger Air Bag \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K65</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"],[2047,31,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>Pins 5 and 24 are connected to\nthe passenger Air Bag disabling switch \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H75</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>When the system self-diagnostic function\ndetects a fault or an impact is detected, control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends\na signal - from pin 13 - to the airbag failure warning light located\nin instrument panel \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . This signal causes the warning light\nto come on because instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied via the ignition\n(INT) from a line protected by the control light fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or by fuse\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              of supplementary fuse box\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              from\n2/99.</p><p>Self-diagnostic data may be read by connecting\nthe unit to connector \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : this receives signals from pin\n9 of control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               through the appropriate tester line.</p><p>Pin 20 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M60</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              sends the signal for\nthe &quot;passenger Air Bag disabled&quot; warning light, located\nin the speedometer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . This signal causes the warning light\nto come on because instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied via the ignition\n(INT) from a line protected by the control light fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or by fuse\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              of supplementary fuse box\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              from\n2/99.</p>"]]